<title>PHILIPPINES: Isuzu unit gets Philippines' BOI nod.</title>
<headline>Isuzu unit gets Philippines' BOI nod.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines' Board of Investments (BOI) had approved a 1.576 billion peso plant of Isuzu Autoparts Manufacturing Corp, a subsidiary of Isuzu Motors Ltd of Japan, documents released on Thursday said.</p>
<p>The facility will produce manual gearboxes for pickup trucks which will both be exported and sold in the domestic markets.</p>
<p>The plant is expected to start commercial operation by May 1998.</p>
<p>A BOI-approved project is eligible for a income tax holiday and preferential tariff on capital equipment, among others.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418938 Fax 8176267</p>
</text>
